From cd221fbd81c0a0ce2a7b0b536edef0885b8d020d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 13:10:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08059/11362] [outer-loop] security audit fix 3/5: confine
 code-executing deserialization

Adds carnot.serialization_safety and routes the 4 pickle.load sites in
python/carnot/verify/ and all 8 torch.load(weights_only=False) sites through it.

CORRECTION to the audit's first pass, which overstated this finding. It reported
"30 of 31 torch.load calls lack weights_only=True". PyTorch 2.6 flipped the
DEFAULT to weights_only=True and this project runs 2.11, so the 22 bare calls
were already safe -- verified empirically: a crafted payload raised
UnpicklingError instead of executing. Only the 8 explicit weights_only=False
sites were ever exposed. The real surface was 12 sites, not 30.

The isinstance() trap, worth naming because it reads as a mitigation and is not:

    loaded = pickle.load(handle)
    if not isinstance(loaded, cls): raise TypeError(...)

A pickle payload executes DURING parsing, so that check runs strictly after the
damage. test_isinstance_check_runs_after_payload_execution proves it with a real
filesystem side effect, so the pattern cannot be reintroduced on the belief that
the type check made it safe. The check is kept via expected_type for its actual
job: catching corruption and wrong-file mistakes.

Two enforcement modes, split by real exposure rather than uniformly:

  refuse (default) -- tier0e_eorm, tier0f_semantic_calibration. Fixed in-repo
      default paths feeding the live verifier ensemble; an out-of-repo path
      there means a live model was redirected at a downloaded file, which is
      exactly the HuggingFace/IPFS mirror supply-chain vector.
  warn -- PartialStateDiffusionScorer, DinaLRMPartialStateScorer. General
      save/load round-trips where a scratch path is ordinary usage.

That split was forced by evidence, not designed up front: refusing everywhere
broke 7 existing tests, and the failing pattern was save(tmp_path) immediately
followed by load(tmp_path) -- a file the same process had just written. No
threat model covers that, so the control was wrong, not the callers. The warn
mode is documented as genuinely weaker: it buys visibility, not prevention.

safe_torch_load attempts weights_only=True FIRST even when the unsafe fallback
is permitted, so allow_unsafe_pickle=True permits a fallback rather than forcing
one -- the warning then identifies which checkpoints still actually need it.

Scope stated honestly in the module docstring: the trusted-root check is no
defence against an attacker who can already write to this repo (they can edit
the source). It blocks the mirror vector and makes every unsafe load greppable.
safetensors is not a drop-in here -- tier0e/tier0f persist fitted scikit-learn
estimators, which are object graphs, not tensor dicts.

13 new tests; all 28 pass across the new suite and the 7 previously-broken ones.

NOTE ON DIFF SIZE: the pre-commit ruff-format hook reformatted regions of the
touched experiment modules that are unrelated to this change. Those files were
not format-clean beforehand, so the reformatting is a precondition of landing
the edit rather than an intentional cleanup.
